    requiredFacts: ['Which tool is this, and what business work do you use it for?', 'Is it used only for the business, or also personally?'],
    answer: 'Monthly or annual software subscriptions used in your work are ordinary business expenses in the year paid. The test is business use: design, accounting, scheduling, storage and similar tools used for the business qualify; a personal streaming plan does not, even if it inspires you. A tool used for both needs a business-use split. An annual prepayment is still deductible when paid under the cash method if the benefit ends within twelve months. Software you buy outright rather than rent is treated like a computer purchase: expense it under the de minimis rule if $2,500 or less, otherwise depreciate. Bundles that include hardware or training should be separated. App-store purchases on a personal account still count if the use is business and you keep the receipt.',
