    answer: 'Rent for a coworking desk, studio or office you use for the business is deductible as business rent in the year paid. Day passes, monthly memberships and dedicated desks all qualify when the space is used for your work; a membership kept mainly for social or personal reasons does not. A deposit is not rent until it is applied to rent or forfeited. Rent paid to a relative must be at a fair market rate. If the space also serves personal purposes, deduct the business share only. Coworking rent does not prevent a home office deduction, but it can affect whether your home is your principal place of business, so keep the two questions separate. Prepaid rent covering more than twelve months ahead is deducted over the period it covers.',
