    answer: 'Parking and tolls paid during business driving are deductible in addition to either vehicle method: the standard mileage rate does not include them. Parking at a client site, a job, a conference or an airport for a business trip qualifies. Parking at your regular work location is commuting and is personal, and so are tolls on the drive from home to that location. Parking tickets and traffic fines are never deductible, even on a business trip. Rideshare and delivery drivers may deduct parking and tolls incurred while working; keep the app trip record as support. Personal errands folded into a business trip are personal, and reimbursed parking is not deductible by you.',
